        "original_id": "70ff62ab-91ae-55ca-8861-8de502e82de3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: The Wars of the Roses (adaptation)\n- People: Roy Dotrice, David Warner, Peggy Ashcroft, Donald Sinden, Paul Hardwick, Janet Suzman, Brewster Mason, Susan Engel, Ian Holm\n- Roles: Henry VI, Margaret of Anjou, Duke of York, Duke of Gloucester, Joan la Pucelle, Earl of Warwick, Edward IV, Queen Elizabeth, Richard III\n\nFacts:\n- Roy Dotrice was born on 26 May 1923 and was a British actor.\n- The production The Wars of the Roses starred David Warner as Henry VI.\n- The production The Wars of the Roses starred Peggy Ashcroft as Margaret of Anjou.\n- The production The Wars of the Roses starred Donald Sinden as the Duke of York.\n- The production The Wars of the Roses starred Paul Hardwick as the Duke of Gloucester.\n- The production The Wars of the Roses starred Janet Suzman as Joan la Pucelle.\n- The production The Wars of the Roses starred Brewster Mason as the Earl of Warwick.\n- The production The Wars of the Roses starred Roy Dotrice as Edward IV.\n- The production The Wars of the Roses starred Susan Engel as Queen Elizabeth.\n- The production The Wars of the Roses starred Ian Holm as Richard III.\n- Roy Dotrice was known for his Tony Award-winning Broadway performance in the revival of A Moon for the Misbegotten.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
